      "decision_index": 78,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Declined to cast Acrobatic Maneuver when they had exactly 3 mana available and no other castable spells this turn. Casting it on Vodalian Arcanist (tapped) would draw a card, untap the Arcanist, and gain 1 life from Distinguished Conjurer's trigger. The cantrip could help find land drops to cast the expensive cards in hand (Teferi, Preston, Chimera all cost 4+). However, saving Acrobatic Maneuver for later synergy with Preston (creating token copies of flickered creatures) is a reasonable consideration.",
      "action_taken": "Passed on casting Acrobatic Maneuver, wasting 3 available mana with no other plays possible this turn.",
      "better_line": "Cast Acrobatic Maneuver targeting Vodalian Arcanist to cantrip (drawing toward land drops for the expensive hand), untap the Arcanist, and gain 1 life. The card draw is especially valuable when the hand is full of 4-5 mana spells and they need lands.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 94,
      "player": "GPT54 Valley",
      "decision_index": 80,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Valley could have blocked Midnight Guard with Distinguished Conjurer and cast Acrobatic Maneuver to exile/return the Conjurer before damage. This would prevent 2 damage, draw a card, gain 1 life from Conjurer's ETB trigger, and keep the Conjurer alive. With exactly 3 untapped lands and no other instant-speed plays affordable, there was no meaningful opportunity cost.",
      "action_taken": "Did not block, taking 2 damage from Midnight Guard",
